G2064.def:
ἔρχομαι, 
[in LXX very frequently for בּוֹא, also for הלךְ ni., אתה, etc., 34 words in all ;] 
__1. to come; 
__(a) of persons, either as arriving or returning from elsewhere: Matthieu 8:9, Marc 6:31, Luc 7:8, Jean 4:27, Romains 9:9, al.; before ἀπό, Marc 5:35 7:1, Jean 3:2, al.; ἐκ, Luc 5:17, Jean 3:31, al.; εἰς, Marc 1:29, al.; διά before εἰς, Marc 7:31; ἐν (Cremer, 263f., but see: ἐν), Romains 15:29, 1 Corinthiens 4:21; ἐπί, with accusative, Marc 6:53 11:13, Jean 19:33, al.; κατά, with accusative, Luc 10:33 Actes 16:7; παρά, with genitive, Luc 8:49; with accusative, Matthieu 15:29, Marc 9:14, al.; with dative comm., incomm. (M, Pr., 75, 245), Matthieu 21:5, Apocalypse 2:5, 16; with adverbs: πόθεν, Jean 3:8, al.; ἄνωθεν, Jean 3:31; ὄπισθεν, Marc 5:27; ὧδε, Matthieu 8:29; ἐκεῖ, Jean 18:3; ποῦ, Hébreux 11:8; before ἕως, Luc 4:42; ἄχρι, Actes 11:5; with purpose expressed by inf., Marc 5:14, Luc 1:59, al.; by fut. ptcp., Matthieu 27:49; ἵνα, Jean 12:9; εἰς τοῦτο, ἵνα, Actes 9:21; διά, with accusative, Jean 12:9; before verbs of action, ἔρχεται καί, ἦλθε καί, etc.: Marc 2:18, Jean 6:15, al.; ἔρχου καὶ ἴδε, Jean 1:47 11:34; ἐλθών (redundant; Dalman, Words, 20 f.), Matthieu 2:8 8:7, Marc 7:25, Actes 16:39, al.; similarly ἐρχόμενος, Luc 15:25, al.; of coming into public view: esp. of the Messiah (ὁ ἐρχόμενος, Matthieu 11:3, al.; see Cremer, 264), Luc 3:16, Jean 4:25; hence, of Jesus, Matthieu 11:19, Luc 7:34, Jean 5:43, al.; of the second coming, Matthieu 10:23, Actes 1:11, 1 Corinthiens 4:5, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:2, al.; 
__(b) of time: ἔρξονται ἡμέραι (present for fut.: Bl., §56, 8), Luc 23:29, Hébreux 8:8" (LXX) ; fut., Matthieu 9:15, Marc 2:20, al.; ἔρξεται ὥρα, ὅτε, Jean 4:21, 23. al.; ἦλθεν, ἐλήλυθε ἡ ὥρα, Jean 13:1 16:32 17:1; ἡ ἡμέρα τ. κυρίου, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:2; καιροί, Actes 3:19; 
__(with) of things and events: κατακλυσμός, Luc 17:27; λιμός, Actes 7:11; ἡ ὀργή, 1 Thessaloniciens 1:10; ὁ λύχνος, Marc 4:21 (see Swete, in l.). Metaphorical, τ. ἀγαθά, Romains 3:8; τ. τέλειον, 1 Corinthiens 13:10; ἡ πίστις, Galates 3:23, 25; ἡ ἐντολή, Romains 7:9; with prepositions: ἐκ τ. θλίψεως, Apocalypse 7:14; ἐις τ. χεῖρον, Marc 5:26; εἰς πειρασμόν, ib. 14:38, al. 
__2. to go: ὀπίσω, with genitive (Heb. הָלַךְ אַחֲרֵי), Matthieu 16:24, Marc 8:34, Luc 9:23; σύν, Jean 21:3; ὁδόν, Luc 2:44. (Cf. ἀν-, ἐπ-αν-, ἀπ-, δι-, εἰς, ἐπ-εἰσ-, συν-εἰσ-, ἐξ-, δι-εξ-, ἐπ-, κατ-, παρ-, ἀντι-παρ-, περι-, προ-, προσ-, συν-έρχομαι.)
SYN.: πορεύομαι, χωρέω (v, Thayer, see word ἔρξομαι).

G2078.def:
ἔσχατος, -η, -ον 
[in LXX chiefly for אַחֲרִית אַחֲרוֹן ;] 
last, utmost, extreme; 
__(a) of place: of the lowest or least honoured place, Luc 14:9-10; τ. ἔσχατον, with genitive part., Actes 1:8 13:47; 
__(b) of time: Matthieu 20:12, 14, Marc 12:6, 22, opposite to πρῶτος, Matthieu 20:8, 1 Corinthiens 15:45, Apocalypse 2:19, al.; τὰ ἔ. καὶ T. πρῶτα, Matthieu 12:45, Luc 11:26, 2 Pierre 2:20; of the Eternal, ὁ πρῶτος καὶ ὁ ἔ., Apocalypse 1:17 2:8 22:13; in phrases relating to the Messianic age and the consummation of the Kingdom of God: ἐπ᾽ ἐσχάτου (-ων) τ. ἡμερῶν, Hébreux 1:2, 2 Pierre 3:3; τ. χρόνων, 1 Pierre 1:20; ἔ. ὥρα, 1 Jean 2:18; ἐπ᾽ ἐ. χόνου, Ju 18; ἐν ἐ. ἡμέραις, Actes 2:17, Jacques 5:3, 2 Timothée 3:1; neut., ἔσχατον, as adv., Marc 12:22, 1 Corinthiens 15:8; 
__(with) of rank: Marc 9:35, 1 Corinthiens 4:9

G2087.def:
ἕτερος, -α, -ον, 
[in LXX chiefly for אַחֵר ;] 
distributive pron., prop. dual (BL, §13, 5; 51, 6), denoting the second of a pair, but in late Gk. encroaching on ἄλλος (M, Pr., 79f.); 
__1. of number, other; with art., the other; 
__(a) of two, Luc 5:7 9:56, al.; opposite to ὁ πρῶτος, Matthieu 21:30; ὁ εἷς, Matthieu 6:24, Luc 7:41, Actes 23:6, al.; ἕ. μὲν . . . ἕ. δέ, the one . . . the other: 1 Corinthiens 15:40; the next: Luc 6:6 9:56 (sc. ἡμέρα, Xen.), Actes 20:15 27:3; = ὁ πλησίον, one's neighbour: Romains 2:1 13:8, 1 Corinthiens 6:1, al.; 
__(b) of more than two, another: Matthieu 8:21 11:3, Luc 6:6 22:65, Jean 19:37, Romains 8:39, al.; pl., Actes 2:13; οἱ μὲν . . . ἄλλοι δὲ . . . ἕ. δέ, Matthieu 16:14; τινὲς . . . ἕ. δέ, Luc 11:16. 
__2. Of kind or quality, other, another, different (Plat., Dem., al.): Mrk.16:[12], Luc 9:29, Actes 2:4, 1 Corinthiens 14:21, 2 Corinthiens 11:4, Galates 1:6, al. (cf. ἑτερό-γλωσσος, -διδασκαλέω, -ζυγέω). 
SYN.: ἄλλος, which see (see reff. ut supr., also Robertson, Gr., 748ff.).

G2089.def:
ἔτι 
adv., 
yet, as yet, still; 
__1. of time; 
__(a) of the present (adhuc): Marc 5:35, 1 Corinthiens 3:3 15:17, Galates 1:10, al.; 
__(b) of the past, mostly with impf.: Matthieu 12:46, Luc 8:49 15:20, Jean 20:1, Actes 9:1, Romains 5:6, 8, 2 Thessaloniciens 2:5, Hébreux 7:10 9:8, al.; 
__(with) of the future: Luc 1:15, 2 Corinthiens 1:10; 
__(d) with a neg.: Matthieu 5:13, Luc 16:2 20:36, Hébreux 10:2, Apocalypse 3:12 20:3, al. 
__2. Of degree, even, yet, still, further: with compar., Philippiens 1:9, Hébreux 7:15; of what remains, Marc 12:6, Jean 4:35 7:33, al.; of what is added, Matthieu 18:16 26:65, Hébreux 11:32 12:26-27; of con­tinuance apart from the idea of time, Romains 3:7 6:2 9:19, Galates 5:11; ἔτι δἐ, Actes 2:26 (LXX), Hébreux 11:36; ἔτι τε καί, Luc 14:26, Actes 21:28

G2090.def:
ἑτοιμάζω
(ἕτοιμος), [in LXX chiefly for כּוּן hi. (Hatch, Essays, 51 a.) ;] 
to prepare, make ready; 
__(a) absol., of hospitable preparation: Marc 14:15, Luc 9:52 12:47 22:9, 12; with inf., Matthieu 26:17; ἵνα, Marc 14:12; 
__(b) with accusative of thing(s): Matthieu 22:4 26:19, Marc 14:16, Luc 12:20 17:8 22:8, 13 23:56 24:1, Jean 14:2-3, Phm 22, Apocalypse 9:7 16:12; before εἰς, 2 Timothée 2:21; of God's ordaining coming events (Dalman, Words, 128); of blessing, Matthieu 20:23 25:34, Marc 10:40, Luc 2:31, 1 Corinthiens 2:9, Hébreux 11:16, Apocalypse 12:6; of judgment, Matthieu 25:41; of preparation for the Messiah, τ. ὁδὸν κυρίου, Matthieu 3:3, Marc 1:3, Luc 1:76 3:4" (LXX) ; 
__(with) with accusative of person(s): Luc 1:17, Actes 23:23, Apocalypse 19:7, before ἵνα, Apocalypse 8:6; εἰς, 2 Timothée 2:21, Apocalypse 9:7, 15 21:2.†

G2092.def:
ἕτοιμος, -ον also (in cl. after Thuc.) -η (2 Corinthiens 9:5, 1 Pierre 1:5), -ον, 
[in LXX chiefly for כּוּן, מָכוֹן (cf. Hatch, Essays, 51 ff.) ;] 
prepared, ready; 
__(a) of things: Matthieu 22:4, 8, Marc 14:15, 2 Corinthiens 9:5 10:16, 1 Pierre 1:5; ἔρχεσθε ὅτι ἤδη ἕτοιμά ἐστιν (Field, Notes, 67), Luc 14:17; ὁ καιρός, Jean 7:6; 
__(b) of persons: Matthieu 24:44 25:10, Luc 12:40, Actes 23:21; before πρός, Tite 3:1, 1 Pierre 3:15; with inf., Luc 22:23; τοῦ, with inf. (WM, § 44, 4a; Robertson, Gr., 1068), Actes 23:15; ἐν ἑ. ἔχω (MM, Exp., xiv), with inf., 2 Corinthiens 10:6.†

G2099.def:
εὐαγγελιστής, -οῦ, ὁ 
an evangelist; 
__(a) in NT, a preacher of the gospel: Actes 21:8, Éphésiens 4:11, 2 Timothée 4:5; 
__(b) later, a writer of a gospel (eccl.).†
